    "### 2.2 The estimation sample\n",
    "\n",
    "1950:4 to 1996:4. The first three quarters are lost to the lags: 1950Q1 has no\n",
    "`dr`, and nothing before 1950Q3 has a `dr_2`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "zs8i63gn",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "rows: 185\n",
      "span: 1950Q4 to 1996Q4\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# the estimation sample: 1950Q4 to 1996Q4, complete rows only\n",
    "sub = df.loc['1950Q4':'1996Q4']\n",
    "sub = sub.dropna(subset=['dr', 'pi_1', 'dy_1', 'dr_1', 'dr_2'])\n",
    "\n",
    "print('rows:', len(sub))                       # 185 usable observations\n",
    "print('span:', sub.index[0], 'to', sub.index[-1])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "q2a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.3 The regression by the classic formula\n",
    "\n",
    "    b = (X'X)^-1 X'y\n",
    "\n",
    "Two things the formula does **not** do for you, both of which `smf.ols` handles\n",
    "quietly: it will not add the intercept, and it will not drop incomplete rows.\n",
    "So the constant has to be a literal column of ones, and `sub` above has to\n",
    "already be the clean sample."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "yi943jkq",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "X: (185, 5)  y: (185,)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "names = ['pi_1', 'dy_1', 'dr_1', 'dr_2']   # this order defines the order of b\n",
    "\n",
    "y = sub['dr'].to_numpy()                   # (n,)\n",
    "X = sub[names].to_numpy()                  # (n, 4) -- no intercept yet\n",
    "\n",
    "n = len(y)\n",
    "ones = np.ones((n, 1))                     # the intercept is a column of ones\n",
    "X = np.hstack([ones, X])                   # (n, 5)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('X:', X.shape, ' y:', y.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "b = np.linalg.inv(X.T @ X) @ X.T @ y       # b = (X'X)^-1 X'y"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "kyptvjtp",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "const -0.2319\n",
      "pi_1 0.0161\n",
      "dy_1 18.3807\n",
      "dr_1 0.2375\n",
      "dr_2 -0.154\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# b is a bare array, so the names have to be put back on\n",
    "labels = ['const'] + names\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, value in zip(labels, b):\n",
    "    print(name, round(value, 4))"
   ]
